- `action(n1, "Start procedure")`: Hallucinates an initial step; the source text begins directly with "Initially, you should check..." and contains no preparatory start procedure. (SMC1)
- `action(n20, "End")`, `action(n23, "End")`, `action(n25, "End")`: Hallucinates explicit termination tasks; the source text states "the process ends", which maps directly to the `end` terminals (`e1`, `e2`, `e3`) without requiring intermediate action nodes. (SMC1)
- `label(n4, c1, "Yes")`: Mislabels the edge triggered when the answer is negative; contradicts `guard(b1, n4, v1 = 'No')` and the source text "Otherwise, continue with the process". (SMC2)